---
import { Icon } from "astro-icon/components";
---

<h3>Challenge: The $50K Cost Crisis</h3>

<div class="bg-red-50 rounded-lg p-6 mb-8 border border-red-200 dark:bg-red-500/10 dark:border-red-600">
  <h4 class="font-semibold mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
    <Icon name="line-md:alert-circle" class="text-red-500" />
    What Happened (Month 4)
  </h4>

  <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-sm">
    <div>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 dark:text-gray-200">We launched beta (380 users). OpenAI bill had potential to explode → <strong>150%</strong>. CFO flagged it, leadership panicked. Had to be remedied in 2 weeks or risk losing funding.</p>

      <p class="text-gray-700 font-semibold mb-2 dark:text-gray-200">My Mistakes:</p>
      <ul class="mb-0 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-200 list-disc not-prose pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>No usage caps (should've had rate limits from day 1)</li>
        <li>Didn't monitor cost metrics daily (only checked monthly)</li>
        <li>Over-optimistic assumptions based on PoC usage patterns</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white/60 rounded-lg p-4 dark:bg-black/20">
      <p class="font-semibold mb-2 text-gray-900 dark:text-white">How I Fixed It:</p>
      <div class="space-y-2">
        <div>
          <strong>Immediate (Day 1):</strong> Emergency rate limits (100 queries/hour/user)
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>Short-term (Week 1):</strong> Cost dashboard with daily alerts if >$2K/day
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>Long-term (Week 2):</strong> I ran 2-week POC with my Staff Engineer on self-hosted Llama 2 70B. Made the call: Migrate to AWS Inferentia.
        </div>
        <div><strong>Result:</strong> <strong>$8K/month (86% reduction)</strong></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-red-300 dark:border-red-600">
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">
      <strong>Lesson I learned:</strong> Cost is a feature for platform teams. Should've built cost tracking into architecture from day 1. Now when I start projects: cost tracking is in acceptance criteria, daily dashboards, alerts if projected monthly cost exceeds threshold.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
